# ‹_2d_chk›  v -> addr   W11-2D: the list-entry mask WITH the use-after-free
# check — `16\shl16>` (strip the tag, or Q's 0x7FFE marker) and then, if the
# length cell holds ⌫'s poison -559038737, `GOLF: use after free` via
# ‹throw›.  No real length is negative, so the poison is unambiguous.  The list
# words (∑ ≢ ⍕ € ⇤ ∏ ⌽ ⌿ ⊐ ⊞ K G, so D and the bare + - * on lists, ≣ ⍤ ⧺ ↑
# ↓ ⍋ ∊ and the W9-4B/4C long words) call it once on entry instead of the bare
# mask; ⊇ (I, the per-element hot path) has its own cheaper inline form.  A
# leaf on the happy path (no scratch); defined here, after U and ‹throw› and
# before L, because it must precede every caller.  The 2D section near the end
# of this file has the rest (‹heapstats›).
