#   ‹close›     fd ->
#   ‹fread›     fd n -> list       ONE read(2) of up to n bytes; empty = EOF
#   ‹fwrite›    list fd ->         write every element's low byte, looping over
#                                  short writes
#   ‹readfile›  path -> list       the whole file
#   ‹writefile› list path ->       create/truncate path, write list, close
# Failure: ‹throw› with `cannot <verb> <path> (<ENAME>)` — verb open, create,
# read, write or close; the fd words name `fd N` instead of a path; an errno
# without a name reads `errno N`.  The positive errno is stored first in the
# 1B errno cell 5179712 (0x4F0940, REGISTRY §3.1); it is never cleared.
