# === W11-2C bind ===
# ⊸ bind (closures by value): x ′f ⊸ -> ′g, where g pushes the CAPTURED x and
# then calls f.  `10→n ←n′+⊸` is a quotation that adds 10 whatever n holds
# later — the value is copied into the code, not the variable's address.  Built
# exactly like ∘ (see the M-CHAIN comment above): a 38-byte thunk in the same
# code arena at 0x4D0000, the same bump pointer 0x4F003C and the same bound,
#   [PROLOGUE][48 B8 x:u64][50][48 B8 f:u64][FF D0][EPILOGUE]
#     sub rbp,8; pop [rbp]  |  mov rax,x; push rax  |  mov rax,f; call rax
#     |  push [rbp]; add rbp,8; ret
# x is any 64-bit value (a tagged list included), so its imm64 is written as
# two 4-byte `!`s, low half then x>>32 (logical shift: `>` never dispatches);
# f is a code address < 2^31, so its high half is 0 as in ∘.  65536-38 = 65498
# is the last legal start offset, so an offset of 65499 or more dies with ∘'s
# message — ∘ and ⊸ share the arena and each checks its own size, so any mix
# of the two is diagnosed before a thunk can reach the variable bank.
# X/Y-wrapped like ∘ (s1 x · s2 f · s3 start), so it may run inside a map.
