# --- W3 hook installation (top-level init; must stay LAST) ---
# M-VEC — implicit vectorization.  The bare + - * ⌈ ⌊ now compile to a
# polymorphic template: it calls through a per-op HOOK CELL when that cell is
# non-zero, and runs the plain scalar op when it is zero (tools/mkblob2._poly).
# The cells are BSS, so installing the five dispatchers below is exactly what
# switches implicit vectorization ON — and why every compiler binary, which
# never runs this prelude, stays byte-for-byte scalar and keeps its fixpoint.
# Cell = 0x4F0100 + 8*op byte (REGISTRY.md §3, stride 8 because the call reads a
# full 64-bit cell):  '+' 0x2B -> 5177944 · '-' 0x2D -> 5177960 ·
# '*' 0x2A -> 5177936 · ⌈ max 0x88 -> 5178688 · ⌊ min 0x89 -> 5178696.
# Each hook is the address of the matching ∔ ∸ ⨰ ⩌ ⩍ word.  Since M-TAG2 the
# template's filter is EXACT — `cmp word [rsp+6],1` / `[rsp+14]`, the same high-
# word test as T — so only a real list operand reaches D; D still re-tests both
# operands and falls back to the raw scalar op, so the hooks would stay correct
# behind a looser filter too.  32-bit `!` is enough —
# BSS leaves each cell's high half zero.  Must stay last: ′ needs the words.
\ref\vadd 5177944!\ref\vsub 5177960!\ref\vmul 5177936!\ref\vmax 5178688!\ref\vmin 5178696!

# === W12-O1 atoms on lists ===
# ‹_12o1_nan›  v -> v   the not-a-number hook of the unary arithmetic atoms
# ± ⊕ ⊖ ² ⊗ ⊘ (cell 0x4F0DC0 = 5180864, tools/mkblob2.NAN_HOOK).  Their
# templates call it only when TOS's top byte is 0x7F, a loose superset of the
# tag; here the test is exact: v is a list iff it is tagged (T) AND its
# address lies in the list heap (addr - base <u span, A's own two cells, the
# test ⌫ makes).  Then `GOLF: not a number` through ‹throw›, so ‹catch› takes
# it.  Anything else — INT64_MAX, any int in the tag band that no heap could
# hold — returns untouched and the atom's scalar body runs on it as before.
# A leaf on the happy path: no scratch, stack-neutral.  The prelude's own
# uses of these atoms are all on ints (lengths, indices, flags), so none of
# them can reach the throw.  Installed LAST, after the W3 hooks, so no init
# code above it can trip the check.
:‹_12o1_nan›"T["16\shl16>5177396@\rsub5177400@\rlt1\radd[“not a number“U‹throw›]];
:‹_12o1_init›\ref‹_12o1_nan›5180864\store;
